<%# Hoojah 2026 threaded response card (mockup hoojah-2026-single-hoojah.html lines
    ~176-231): a rounded `bg-card` card with a 6px stance-coloured LEFT border strip —
    the signature Hoojah motif — the responder's byline (name · @handle · stance · time),
    the argument body, and a stance-tally footer.

    Response filter: the card is the filter's item — `data-response-filter-target="item"`
    / `data-response-filter-vote="<stance>"`. `response_filter_controller` matches those by
    string against `_response_filter` and `_challenge_dialog`; they stay spelled exactly and
    now live on the container <div> (the controller selects by data-target, not by tag —
    Slice B moved them off the old <a>). Stance names are interpolated into `bg-<stance>` /
    `text-<stance>` (all in the @source inline safelist); the `-soft` pairs come from a
    literal lookup (below) so no new interpolated prefix ships.

    Slice B (hovercard): the card is NO LONGER a single outer <a>. To give the responder's
    avatar + name their own profile link + hovercard trigger without nesting an <a> in an
    <a>, this uses the stretched-link pattern — the container is a `relative` <div>, the
    hoojah link is an inset overlay anchor (`absolute inset-0 z-0`, empty body, aria-label
    carries the response snippet), and the avatar/name byline are `ui/_user_link`s lifted
    above the overlay with `relative z-10`. The @handle · stance · time caption stays plain
    (wrapping the time in a profile anchor would be wrong). A click anywhere else on the
    card still opens the response's own page. Still no menu inside the card (a flag menu
    would nest a form/anchor) — the flag surface remains the response's own show page.

    Locals: child (the response hoojah), hujah (the root claim), and the optional
    `live_debate_keys` set (from `_response_filter`) used to show the "In debate" badge.

    The "Challenge to debate" affordance and the "In debate" badge render OUTSIDE the card
    anchor (a nested <a> is invalid HTML) — CompactHujahCard.prompt.md: "renders below the
    card, never inside it". Each carries the same response-filter item+vote so it hides in
    sync with its card. The challenge affordance is gated to a signed-in non-author AND
    `hujah.allow_debates?` (2026). When the response already has a live/pending debate the
    badge replaces the challenge trigger.

    2026 Phase 3.2: the affordance is a plain LINK to the debate create page
    (`new_hujah_debate_path`), not the stance-only `hujahs/_challenge_dialog` <dialog> it
    used to open — that partial is kept on disk (its FROZEN block documents what still
    points at it) but nothing renders it from here any more. The create page collects the
    stance itself, so this link carries no `challenger_stance`. %>
<% stance = {1 => "agree", 2 => "neutral", 3 => "disagree"}[child.vote] || "primary" %>
<% soft = {
     "agree" => "bg-agree-soft text-agree",
     "neutral" => "bg-neutral-soft text-neutral",
     "disagree" => "bg-disagree-soft text-disagree",
     "primary" => "bg-primary-soft text-primary"
   }[stance] %>
<% in_debate = local_assigns[:live_debate_keys]&.include?([child.user_id, child.vote]) %>
<%# Coerce ONCE here (absent-or-nil on the create-stream / missing-local path → 0),
    so the guard and the pluralize below read the same integer. %>
<% reply_count = local_assigns[:reply_count].to_i %>
<%# Favourites (2026). `can_favourite` (parent author viewing their own thread) and
    `favourite_counts` ({vote => starred count}) come from `_response_filter`; both are
    absent on the create-stream path, which then renders no star control. A FULL stance
    hides the "add" star on its unstarred replies — the model still enforces the cap. %>
<% favourited = child.favourited? %>
<% show_star_toggle = local_assigns[:can_favourite] && Hujah::STANCES.key?(child.vote) &&
     (favourited || local_assigns[:favourite_counts].to_h.fetch(child.vote, 0) < Hujah::FAVOURITES_PER_STANCE) %>
<div class="relative block mb-2.5"
     data-response-filter-target="item" data-response-filter-vote="<%= stance %>">
  <%= link_to hujah_path(child.slug), class: "absolute inset-0 z-0",
        "aria-label": "Response: #{truncate(strip_tags(child.body.to_s), length: 90)}" do %><% end %>
  <div class="flex overflow-hidden rounded-2xl bg-card shadow">
    <div class="w-1.5 shrink-0 bg-<%= stance %>"></div>
    <div class="flex-1 min-w-0 p-3.5">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
        <%= render layout: "ui/user_link", locals: {user: child.user, class: "relative z-10 shrink-0"} do %>
          <%= render "ui/avatar", user: child.user, size: :sm %>
        <% end %>
        <div class="flex flex-col min-w-0 leading-tight">
          <%= render layout: "ui/user_link", locals: {user: child.user, class: "relative z-10 block text-sm font-bold text-ink truncate"} do %><%= child.user.full_name %><% end %>
          <div class="text-xs text-ink-2">
            @<%= child.user.username %>
            <% if child.vote %>
              <span class="mx-0.5">·</span>
              <span class="font-bold text-<%= stance %>"><%= stance.capitalize %></span>
            <% end %>
            <span class="mx-0.5">·</span>
            <time datetime="<%= child.created_at.iso8601 %>" data-local="time-ago"><%= child.created_at.strftime("%b %-d") %></time>
          </div>
        </div>
        <%# The star sits above the stretched-link overlay (`relative z-10`) so it is
            its own target. The parent author gets a toggle; everyone else sees a
            read-only marker on a starred reply. `form: {class: "contents"}` keeps the
            button_to wrapper out of the flex layout. %>
        <% if show_star_toggle %>
          <%= button_to hujah_favourite_path(child.slug),
                method: (favourited ? :delete : :post),
                form: {class: "contents"},
                class: "relative z-10 ml-auto shrink-0 p-1 rounded-full cursor-pointer active:scale-95 #{favourited ? "text-primary" : "text-faint"}",
                title: (favourited ? "Unfavourite" : "Favourite"),
                aria: {label: (favourited ? "Unfavourite response" : "Favourite response"), pressed: favourited} do %>
            <%= lucide_icon("star", class: "w-5 h-5 #{"fill-current" if favourited}") %>
          <% end %>
        <% elsif favourited %>
          <span data-testid="favourite-marker" class="relative z-10 ml-auto shrink-0 inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-xs font-bold text-primary" title="Favourited by @<%= hujah.user.username %>">
            <%= lucide_icon("star", class: "w-4 h-4 fill-current") %> Author's pick
          </span>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink break-words"><%= format_body(child.body) %></div>
      <%# Secret ballot (2a/A7): the per-stance tally is a de-anonymization vector below
          k=3 total votes — replaced by the total-only label until the electorate grows. %>
      <div class="mt-3 flex items-center gap-4 text-xs text-ink-2 font-semibold">
        <% if child.breakdown_visible? %>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1"><%= stance_icon("agree", class: "w-3.5 h-3.5") %><%= child.agree_count.to_i %></span>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1"><%= stance_icon("neutral", class: "w-3.5 h-3.5") %><%= child.neutral_count.to_i %></span>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1"><%= stance_icon("disagree", class: "w-3.5 h-3.5") %><%= child.disagree_count.to_i %></span>
        <% else %>
          <span><%= vote_total_label(child) %></span>
        <% end %>
        <%# Reply-thread presence: a subtle signal that this response has its own
            visible replies (count mirrors visible_children_for — removed/blocked/
            private-author grandchildren are excluded). `reply_count` is threaded
            in from `_response_filter` (one grouped query for the whole row) — a
            plain integer, absent-or-0 for responses with no visible replies. The
            card already navigates to the response's own page, so this needs no
            separate link. %>
        <% if reply_count > 0 %>
          <span data-testid="reply-count" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1"><%= lucide_icon("message-circle", class: "w-3.5 h-3.5") %><%= pluralize(reply_count, "reply") %></span>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<% if in_debate %>
  <div data-response-filter-target="item" data-response-filter-vote="<%= stance %>"
       class="flex justify-end -mt-1 mb-2.5 pr-2">
    <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold <%= soft %>">
      <%= lucide_icon("swords", class: "w-3.5 h-3.5") %> In debate
    </span>
  </div>
<% elsif user_signed_in? && current_user.id != child.user_id && hujah.allow_debates? %>
  <div data-response-filter-target="item" data-response-filter-vote="<%= stance %>"
       class="flex justify-end -mt-1 mb-2.5 pr-2">
    <%= link_to new_hujah_debate_path(hujah, argument_id: child.id),
          class: "#{ds_button_classes(variant: :link, tone: "neutral")} text-xs" do %>
      <%= lucide_icon("swords", class: "w-3.5 h-3.5") %> Challenge to debate
    <% end %>
  </div>
<% end %>
